---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial policy"
  description="How Sorlio Guides chooses topics, writes comparisons, checks facts, handles corrections and discloses its relationship with Sorlio."
  path="/editorial-policy/"
  current="about"
>
  <div class="prose-wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About', href: '/about/' }, { label: 'Editorial policy' }]} />
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">How {SITE.name} decides what to publish, how comparisons are made, and how we handle mistakes.</p>

    <h2>Our relationship with Sorlio</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is published by the makers of Sorlio, an Android app. We are not an independent review
      organisation. Every guide that mentions Sorlio says so, and comparison guides state how they were made.
    </p>

    <h2>How topics are chosen</h2>
    <p>
      We write about questions learners actually ask, such as which kind of app suits them, how to read French at their
      level, and how to use news or stories for practice. We do not publish articles that exist only to rank for a
      product name without answering the question.
    </p>

    <h2>How comparisons are made</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Comparisons use public information about each product, and the method is stated on the page.</li>
      <li>We group products by learner need rather than publishing a single overall ranking.</li>
      <li>We do not claim to have tested products or measured learning outcomes unless we have.</li>
      <li>Where another product suits a learner better, the guide says so.</li>
      <li>Prices and plan limits are shown only when they have been checked against an official source, with a date.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How facts are checked</h2>
    <p>
      Claims about learning are supported with references where we can give them accurately. Claims about products are
      checked against official pages before publication where possible. Where a claim has not been checked, the guide
      does not state it as fact, or it says the reader should check the current details.
    </p>

    <h2>Authors and reviewers</h2>
    <p>
      Guides are written by the Sorlio team. We do not list individual author biographies or qualifications.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>No reviewer has been named, and no French teacher or native speaker has reviewed these guides.</strong>
      The French examples and practice passages were written by us and checked for grammar, but they have not been
      checked by a teacher. Treat them as learning material, not as an authoritative reference.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and updates</h2>
    <p>
      Each guide shows its publication date and, where it has changed substantially, a last-updated date. If we find an
      error, we correct it and update the date. If you spot a mistake, please tell us so we can fix it.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising, affiliates and data</h2>
    <p>
      The site contains no affiliate links, advertising and tracking scripts. Links to Sorlio on Google Play are the only
      links that lead to a product we publish. See the <a href="/about/">About and disclosure</a> page for more.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
